open-forge:
  description: Active plan and delegated fixes for four Neon Pairs regressions
  tags: [Memory, Working, Contextual]
---

# Game regressions

User request: fix best scores, arrow navigation, reduced motion and unwanted audio while following `docs/README.md`. Plan first; give each fix to a distinct subagent. The primary agent reviews and verifies but edits no code.

Plan: delegate in order to four agents because one subagent slot is available. Each agent reads the loader and project requirements, fixes its behavior and adds or runs focused regression checks. Then run the locked install, type checks, unit/static tests, fresh-build browser journeys and formatting checks.

Observed causes: `rememberBest` always overwrote; `GameStatus` used zero for an absent best; board focus had no arrow handler; card and status styles lacked reduced-motion overrides; `use-game.ts` created audio on matches and wins. All four were corrected in their owning modules.

Initial Git tree is clean. Use `git -c safe.directory=/work` for Git reads. Node 26.12.1 and npm 11.20.0 are available; dependencies and browser availability need verification.

Best-score fix completed by its subagent: `rememberBest` now preserves an equal or lower existing result; the status shows `none` if the selected size has no completed record. Existing unit and browser tests cover better/equal/worse results, storage round trips, persistence after reload, size separation, and the absent-record label. Focused storage/session unit tests (17) and the full typecheck pass.

Keyboard fix completed by its subagent: `useBoardFocus` handles unmodified arrow movement within rows and columns, stops at edges, and marks keyboard focus visibly. Focused browser journeys for keyboard completion, edge stops, Tab exit, large boards, scroll and focus rings passed (12 tests); typecheck and build passed.

Reduced-motion fix completed: `card.css` disables card transitions and `status.css` disables the win pulse under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`. `npm run build` passed, and both `tests/motion.e2e.test.ts` browser checks passed on the named Chromium runtime.

Silence fix completed: removed the Web Audio tone path while retaining clock synchronization and game activation. Source audit (3 tests), build/typecheck, and all 3 `browser-environment` tests passed on Node 26.12.1, npm 11.20.0, Playwright 1.64.1 and Chromium 156.0.8078.4. The browser checks confirmed mismatch timing, storage fallback, and silent match/win/restart play.

Next: run combined typecheck, unit tests, fresh build/browser journeys, and formatting checks; review every diff. All work is local; no commits or publication requested.

